/* book exam traps: Taking the TCR output as the SVC output. The TCR only absorbs vars; the fixed capacitor supplies leading vars; the net SVC output is the difference BC − BL(α). | Putting α in degrees inside the formula. Convert to radians first. Keep the sign: sin 240° = −0.866. | Mixing SVC and STATCOM V-I behaviour. An SVC at its limit looks like a fixed susceptance, so current falls with voltage. A STATCOM holds current up to its limit, so it gives more reactive current at low voltage. | Treating UPFC as a shunt-only SVC. A UPFC has a shunt converter and a series converter, and the series converter is what controls line power flow. */
